  "intro": "These Houston listings were checked on Public Storage’s own facility pages on November 20, 2026, and cover eleven locations inside the Loop or just off it: North Loop West, the Washington Ave corridor, W Gray and Westheimer near Montrose and River Oaks, Upper Kirby, Highland Village, Midtown, Almeda Rd in the Museum District, and two Old Spanish Trail sites near the Texas Medical Center. We copied published access hours and office hours separately, and we only flag climate control when the facility’s own page lists it. None of these facilities published around-the-clock access hours: three pages show a “24/7 Access Available” badge, but their access-hours tables are 6:00 AM–10:00 PM, and two facilities near Montrose and River Oaks close access at 6:00 PM on weekdays (one at 5:00 PM on weekends). This is a starting sample from one operator, not a citywide inventory; suburbs such as Katy, Sugar Land, Pearland, and The Woodlands are not included yet, and we do not cache live unit prices or vacancy.",
